<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sam Khubis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1915</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sam Khubis was fought on 8 May 1915 in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rehoboth-namibia">Rehoboth</a> Basters and German colonial troops. After the Basters refused to fight against the advancing South African forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, German troops attacked them at the mountain of Sam Khubis, but the assault was broken off. The Basters commemorate the day every year as one of deliverance.</p></div>
